Chapter: ArcSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Pose
  cites Safari chapter Bike
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter Arc
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Arc: run the bike's physics forward from where the rider is and report where he
 would leave the road, if he would.

 IT IS A SIMULATION WITH FOUR WAYS OUT and each one answers a different record.
 He runs off the left shoulder, off the right, far enough forward to be safe, or
 the loop runs out of steps. The first two are the answer the shoulder brake
 acts on; the last two are both "no shoulder" and are NOT the same event, which
 is why `frames` is the placeholder in both and `forward` is not.

 THE PLACEHOLDER IS GRADED AS A VALUE. `no-frames` is 1e9, and the chapter says
 outright it is what the zig stores rather than a number anyone reads -- the
 brake only looks at `frames` when the shoulder is not none. Grading it is what
 keeps a rewrite from "tidying" it to zero, which would read as a rider leaving
 the road on frame nought.

 A RIDER WITH NO LEAN GOES EXACTLY STRAIGHT, which is what makes this gradeable
 at 0.0 without a tolerance anywhere. `simulate-rider-step` moves him by
 `v * r-sin mid`, and with no tilt the mid-heading is zero and the sine of zero
 is EXACTLY zero -- an odd polynomial at the origin -- so his across never
 changes at all. His along creeps by `v * r-cos 0`, which is not exact, but the
 forward answer is clamped to `min-forward-progress` before it is reported.

 THE BOUNDS WIDEN TO WHERE HE ALREADY IS, and that is the case worth having: a
 rider outside the inset is not instantly judged to have left the road. Graded
 with a rider three metres off centre on a four-metre lane, which is well past
 the 1.95 inset and still not a departure.

 We say:

Section: The Constants

  fixed-got : List Real
  fixed-got = [no-frames, straighten-margin, min-forward-progress]

  fixed-want : List Real
  fixed-want = [1000000000.0, 0.05, 25.0]

  steps-got : List Integer
  steps-got = [turn-danger-steps]

  steps-want : List Integer
  steps-want = [2000]

Section: Riding It Out

  seg : Segment
  seg = segment-at 0

  rider : Real, Real, Real -> RiderState
  rider (across) (tilt) (v) =
    RiderState { segment = 0, along = 0.0, across = across, yaw = 0.0, v = v,
                 tilt = tilt, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }

  side : ArcOutcome -> Integer
  side (o) =
    when o.shoulder
     is ShoulderLeft -> -1
     is ShoulderNone -> 0
     is ShoulderRight -> 1

 Straight down the middle at the base speed: he never leaves, and the run stops
 the moment he is twenty-five metres clear rather than after two thousand steps.

  straight : ArcOutcome
  straight = project-arc (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base) seg

  straight-got : List Real
  straight-got = [straight.forward, straight.end-across, straight.frames]

  straight-want : List Real
  straight-want = [25.0, 0.0, 1000000000.0]

 Off centre and still straight: the bounds widened to where he is, so three
 metres out on a four-metre lane is not a departure.

  wide : ArcOutcome
  wide = project-arc (rider 3.0 0.0 v-base) seg

  wide-got : List Real
  wide-got = [wide.forward, wide.end-across, wide.frames]

  wide-want : List Real
  wide-want = [25.0, 3.0, 1000000000.0]

 A rider going nowhere makes no forward progress and never leaves either, so the
 loop runs out of steps -- a different way to reach the same shoulder and a
 different `forward`.

  stopped : ArcOutcome
  stopped = project-arc (rider 0.0 0.0 0.0) seg

  stopped-got : List Real
  stopped-got = [stopped.forward, stopped.end-across, stopped.frames]

  stopped-want : List Real
  stopped-want = [0.0, 0.0, 1000000000.0]

  none-got : List Integer
  none-got = [side straight, side wide, side stopped]

  none-want : List Integer
  none-want = [0, 0, 0]

  crossed-got : List Boolean
  crossed-got = [straight.crossed, wide.crossed, stopped.crossed]

  crossed-want : List Boolean
  crossed-want = [False, False, False]

Section: Leaving It

 A lean tips the heading and the heading walks him sideways. The sign of the
 tilt is the sign of the shoulder he leaves by, and both are graded -- a
 chapter that lost the sign would still report a departure every time.

  leaning : ArcOutcome
  leaning = project-arc (rider 0.0 0.2 v-base) seg

  other-way : ArcOutcome
  other-way = project-arc (rider 0.0 (0.0 - 0.2) v-base) seg

  leaving-got : List Integer
  leaving-got = [side leaning, side other-way]

  leaving-want : List Integer
  leaving-want = [1, -1]

 A departure reports the frame it happened on rather than the placeholder, and
 it is inside the step budget. Its forward is clamped at the same
 twenty-five-metre ceiling a safe run reports.

  left-got : List Boolean
  left-got =
    [ leaning.frames < no-frames,
      leaning.frames < real-from-int turn-danger-steps,
      leaning.frames > 0.0,
      leaning.forward <= min-forward-progress,
      leaning.end-across > 0.0,
      other-way.end-across < 0.0,
      other-way.frames < no-frames ]

  left-want : List Boolean
  left-want = [True, True, True, True, True, True, True]

 The two leans are mirror images, so they leave on the same frame by opposite
 sides -- a stronger statement than either one alone, and it needs no number
 written down. The frame and the across mirror EXACTLY, because the sine is odd
 to the last bit at these arguments; the forward does not, because the cosine's
 polynomial is not exactly even and the along accumulates it once per frame.

  mirror-got : List Real
  mirror-got =
    [ leaning.frames - other-way.frames,
      leaning.end-across + other-way.end-across ]

  mirror-want : List Real
  mirror-want = [0.0, 0.0]

  mirror-fwd-got : List Real
  mirror-fwd-got = [leaning.forward - other-way.forward]

  mirror-fwd-want : List Real
  mirror-fwd-want = [0.0]

Section: One Step

 The physics underneath, on its own: no lean means no turn, so the across is
 untouched and the yaw and heading do not move. The lean-to-yaw ratio is a tenth.

  step-got : List Real
  step-got =
    let a = simulate-rider-step (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base) 0.0 0.0
    in let b = simulate-rider-step (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base) 0.5 0.25
    in [ a.across, a.yaw, a.heading, a.tilt, a.v,
         b.tilt, b.v, b.yaw, b.heading, yaw-per-tilt ]

  step-want : List Real
  step-want = [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.55, 0.05, 0.05, 0.1]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-fixed " fixed-got fixed-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "ar-steps " steps-got steps-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-straig" straight-got straight-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-wide  " wide-got wide-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-stop  " stopped-got stopped-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "ar-none  " none-got none-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ar-cross " crossed-got crossed-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "ar-side  " leaving-got leaving-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "ar-left  " left-got left-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-mirror" mirror-got mirror-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-mfwd  " mirror-fwd-got mirror-fwd-want 0.000001)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "ar-step  " step-got step-want 0.0)
  end
